{"kind":"request","text":"Archive: operator restart of a row stopped with reason limit.\nOld stopped rows have no record of the cause, so the deferred-for-capacity change does not bring them back. The stopped row on object c7a17b72 on dap-grow needs a restart path.\nWork, as proposed in 6ffc771a: add a distinct operator transition from stopped to retry. Do this after the deferred-for-capacity request.","body":{"conditions":"(1) The transition names the exact mapped scope and repository, and refuses any other. (2) It requires a confirmed-v2 receipt and no pending Mark. (3) It uses a compare-and-set on the canonical row. (4) It keeps the receipt and frontier fields, and restores the normal retry wake in the same write. (5) Only the operator can run it. (6) A witness runs the real operator path. (7) Gate once before review; exact-head checker review before the planner deploys and runs it.","priority":"normal","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}